{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-18T13:39:53.220Z","data":{"text":"Task 6 complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented OpenSpec-compatible archival in `src/watcher/archiver.ts`, with tests in `tests/archiver.test.ts`.\n\n**Acceptance coverage (10/10 task tests pass; repo gate `tsc + 395 tests + lint` clean):**\n\n1. **Configured archive path** — `archiveSpecFolder` moves to `config.paths.archive`, verified under both legacy (`specs/archive`) and OpenSpec (`openspec/changes/archive`).\n2. **Full history preserved** — single `rename` moves the whole `.run/` tree; test asserts `approved`, `done/`, `results/`, and `events/` survive.\n3. **Deterministic delta application during archive** — `applyDelta` now runs inside `archiveSpecFolder` (moved out of `checkAndArchiveSpec` so ADDED is applied exactly once) and merges into `openspec/specs/<capability>/spec.md`.\n4. **Archived `tasks.md` fully ticked** — new `tickAllTaskCheckboxes` + recursive `ensureArchivedTasksTicked` rewrite every `[ ]` to `[x]`, preserving bullets/numbering/indentation.\n5. **Both paths tested** — explicit legacy and OpenSpec archival tests.\n\n**Notable deviations:** full `applyDelta` (OpenSpec + legacy prose) is used to preserve existing behavior; ticking runs on the moved copy; only files named `tasks.md` are touched (never task-unit acceptance checklists). `paths.openspecRoot` isn't in the working tree (`OsqPaths` still lacks it), so the existing defensive accessor and `paths.archive` drive OpenSpec behavior without editing out-of-scope `config.ts`.\n\nResult written to `specs/016-openspec-artifacts/.run/results/6.md`."}}
